WEBVTT

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.140
Rook...

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.060
You're late, Kaito.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:52.900
Lost

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.030
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.950
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.830
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.210
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.920
Found

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.130
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:15.630
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.430
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.560
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.890
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.770
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.480
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.860
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.070
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:35.440
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.910
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.620
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.450
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.290
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.460
It's now or never

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.540
That is what they say

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.630
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:54.300
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.460
That is what they say

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.630
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.140
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.350
That is what they say

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.770
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.980
The Promise

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.160
First game, winner:

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.070
Miss Melancholy.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:25.080
You've got a long way to
go before you can beat me.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.710
Right, right, Big Sis?

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.480
I've gotten what I wanted.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.840
I'm grateful for the cooperation.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.920
Now all that's left is to wait for
Upperclassman Souji's transmission.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.860
Kaito, I will have you make good.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.530
By this pendant, the
promise you made to me.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.990
Promise?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.860
What does he mean?

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:06.330
Moving on, the second
game shall now begin.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.340
Whoa!

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.540
The slider's arrangement changed.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.210
Next up...

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.880
it's my and Kaito's turn.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.850
Kaito Daimon's opponent is
Pinochle, of all people.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:29.980
This game won't be very
cute, will it, Sis?

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.510
If I should lose,

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:36.690
would you young ladies let
me cry upon your laps?

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:38.600
I don't think so.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.510
How cold.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.280
I guess I'll just have to win.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.330
Klondike will be watching.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.510
I'm not nervous at all.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.330
I'm the type that heats up
when attention's on him.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.840
Do not sully the name
of the Orpheus Order.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.730
All I have to do is win, right?

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.550
Winning will gain anyone's forgiveness.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.760
Right, Freecell?

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.100
I wish you good fighting, Pinochle.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.380
Kaito!

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.890
Good luck!

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.510
Mr. Kaito goes first.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:34.460
Now then, second game...

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.960
Play.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.010
I'll get on the neighboring slider next.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.790
If I do, he'll probably...

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.110
I thought as much.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.070
What?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.830
That goof down there is somethin' else!

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:57.990
Again...

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.060
And again!

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.550
The next one he'll move to is...

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.180
I knew it! He's reading my intentions!

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.280
He's reading Kaito's intentions?

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.560
Yeah, no doubt about it.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.190
It looks like he's investigated
Kaito thoroughly.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:30.200
That's right, Kaito Daimon,
all your data is in my head!

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.390
Your life.

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.080
Your everything.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:38.210
How you've solved every
puzzle up till now.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:44.900
You solve things so elegantly, don't you?

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.430
This is Pinochle's greatest weapon.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:53.210
Every single puzzle from
all ages and cultures...

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:56.680
The thoughts, the experiences
of the opponent...

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:01.730
He expertly researches all
data to create his strategy.

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:05.230
It really is unbeatable.

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:09.350
Still, he has no sense of pride.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:12.240
How he solves things isn't cute, is it?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.990
Well, what will you do, Kaito?

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:22.700
I know just what you're thinking.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.710
Next is...

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:40.260
Kaito...

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:43.690
Next...

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.370
Next...

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.700
Next...

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.780
Next!

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.280
Dammit!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.740
Next is...

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.160
No need to worry, Nonoha!

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.320
That fool Kaito's gonna pull it off!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:38.160
What is this sensation?

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:42.580
Next...

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.550
Don't tell me!

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.210
Next...

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.220
I...

00:08:58.650 --> 00:08:59.740
Next...

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.100
Next...

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.030
I'm...

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:16.530
being moved!

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:20.630
Kaito Daimon is reading
Pinochle's intentions!

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:25.060
More precisely, he's reading what
Pinochle had read from him,

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:27.540
and is then reading from that.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.690
Then, this "Pinochle" person's data is...

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:33.670
Yeah, it don't apply to Kaito anymore.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.970
Then, Kaito has won!

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.630
All right, go, Kaito!

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.560
I, Ana, think you should go for it!

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.060
Good luck!
Keep it up, Kaito!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:51.070
Such raucous noise!

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.320
Freecell...

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.580
In one blow...

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.710
I'm gonna finish him off!

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:13.800
Rook Banjo Crossfield...

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:22.050
Parting with Rook was
quite painful, wasn't it?

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.060
It's started.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:29.400
Huh?

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:30.560
What's this?

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.830
It was the night of a full moon.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:40.340
You two had slipped from school
and gone to Great Henge.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:44.150
After that, you never
saw him again, did you?

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.190
How...

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.800
How do you know that?

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:52.080
Calm down, Kaito!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.300
A group like the Orpheus Order would

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.580
be able to research that easily.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:00.590
Easily?

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:01.910
That's right.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.890
They may have hacked the POG's data.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.840
I told you, didn't I?

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:10.600
Everything about you
is in my head, Kaito.

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:14.170
Incidentally, you had Nonoha's special

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.400
rice omelet for dinner last night.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:17.740
Huh?

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.730
It had a little too much
salt, right, Nonoha?

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.410
H..How...

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.530
Kaito, when you took a shower last night,

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:28.730
you were out of shampoo, weren't you?

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:30.090
That won't do.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.500
You need to buy replacements
ahead of time.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.120
He's right!

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:36.130
How do you know that?!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.760
Wait, how do you?

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.190
The POG wouldn't have
that data, would they?

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:44.260
But I can see everything.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.730
I...

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:48.480
Rather, Freecell and the others,

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:51.890
we were students of Crossfield Academy.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.520
We were in the same building as you,
spent time together.

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:59.070
Though it seems you don't remember that.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.250
You were special back then.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.210
You were the genius transfer
student from the East.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:11.460
You could solve any puzzle easily,

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.510
and always had a bored look on your face.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:23.130
Your eyes looked as if they
were watching insects.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.170
No...

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:30.560
Your eyes watched us as if
we weren't there at all.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:32.440
That ain't true!

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:36.560
You'd just lost your parents, hadn't you?

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.990
It's only natural that
you'd close off your heart.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:44.320
But does that give you
the right to hurt others?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:48.020
Hurt others?

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:49.490
I did?

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:05.900
That puzzle was great, huh?

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.560
Yeah, awesome!

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.070
You're Kaito Daimon?

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:17.020
They say you're good at solving puzzles.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.120
We're all about to do some puzzles.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:22.270
Wanna join us, Kaito?

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.540
This is my pride and joy.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:26.980
It took second place
in the championships.

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:31.890
Is he really that good?

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:33.840
They're just rumors, right?

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:37.630
Try solving this.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.780
H..He even got to six.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.810
He already solved it...

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:08.090
Let's go, guys.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:15.470
You were all alone, yet
you wounded the children

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:17.300
who tried to play with you.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.880
"Wounded them," you say?

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:22.000
All he did was solve their puzzles!

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:24.210
He didn't do anything bad!

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:27.170
Yes, Kaito's not "bad."

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:29.600
Those children were simply
at too low a level,

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.970
unable to be Kaito's opponents.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.010
That's not it!

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:38.030
But finally, you were
able to make a friend.

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:41.770
Yes, you brought misfortune even to Rook.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.640
One day, you became absorbed in a puzzle

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:48.530
and forgot your promise to Rook.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.040
Oh, no!

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:06.260
I'm sorry, Rook!

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.710
Because of that your return was delayed,

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:13.930
and the lab people
noticed Rook was absent.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:16.220
And then...

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.950
It's your fault, isn't it?

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:23.150
It's your fault Rook went
down the wrong path,

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:26.480
and that Nonoha and the others
have faced such danger.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.320
Shut up! That don't involve you!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.520
The puzzle...

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:32.910
I'm continuing the puzzle!

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.410
That's the kind of person you are.

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.670
Now, as then,

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:50.500
you wound others while you have fun
solving puzzles alone.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:55.180
You like puzzles more than people.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.120
Kaito's not like that!

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:58.930
Yes!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.490
You can't even remember, can you?

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:07.440
There's one more person
here that you've wounded.

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:12.200
What do you mean?

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.660
Promise...

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.790
Wounded...

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:46.980
It looks like you've
remembered, about him.

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:51.490
But I never spoke to him, not once!

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.990
You have, just once.

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:56.370
What?

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.460
That's when you made your promise.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.160
U..Um, Kaito?

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.930
Huh? Do a puzzle together?

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:15.710
Sure.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.370
Okay, see you Monday.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:26.900
He waited so long.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.510
Yet you...

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.370
That day...

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:35.920
That day, I...

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:39.220
That's when Rook disappeared.

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:42.270
I thought I could see him
if I went to Great Henge.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.040
And then...

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.500
You forgot, your promise with him.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:55.880
Do you know how sad you made him?

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:57.800
His mother as well.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.180
Mother?

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.680
Sad...

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.210
Sad...

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:11.190
What is it, Melancholy?

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:15.190
She died sad.

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:17.700
She died?

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:20.370
Don't let 'em fool ya, Kaito!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:23.290
This is just a bunch of lies!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.540
That's right!

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.570
Is that true?

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:29.040
Was it really my fault?

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.250
In the midst of your sadness...

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.990
you made Mama die.

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:08.000
What does that mean?

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.240
What is it?

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:21.280
I thought you were resuming the game.

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:27.190
Kaito...

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:29.300
What a damn, dirty trick!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.230
It's unforgiveable!

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:35.730
Though Klondike is watching...

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.240
What an unsightly game this is!

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:43.700
Dammit! Where should I go?

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.350
It's your turn.

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.250
Hurry, hurry!

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.290
This move...

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.530
Kaito Daimon can win in two turns!

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:58.280
Really, Cube?!

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.800
Pr..Probably...

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:01.720
No.

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.480
Too bad.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:17.850
That's the end.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:20.090
Second game, winner:

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.490
Mr. Pinochle.

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:22.970
Huh?!

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.490
But he hasn't won yet!

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:26.620
It's over.

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.280
Even if he were to continue...

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:33.620
Goofy down there would
get to the goal first.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:35.630
There's no way Kaito can win.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:37.420
Oh, no!

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.960
Kaito lost?

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:44.050
Kaito...

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:53.060
Let us have a brief rest
before the next game.

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:08.250
I made her die?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.580
Freecell!

00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:18.840
You saw, right?

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:22.340
Kaito Daimon remembered you!

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:26.220
I made him remember!

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.320
Thank you, Pinochle.

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:30.720
But...

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.230
Kaito would have remembered without

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:44.650
someone like you butting in.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.190
He would have remembered!

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:50.410
Fr..Freecell!

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:53.500
The one who'll begin
puzzle time with Kaito

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:55.610
is me.

